/// This source transports `true` along the negation composite at three
/// lengths of cctt's `tests/bench/negPath.cctt`.
///
/// The composite at `n` holds `n + 1` negation paths, so an even `n` moves
/// `true` to `false`. A path between types runs as its two maps. So each run
/// applies negation once for each path of the composite.
///
/// The run machine runs each length that this source states. At 10⁶ the run
/// spends its fuel budget.
///
/// - see: #6309
/// - see: #6325 — the fuel budget at 10⁶
// The natural numbers.
import "./circle-base.gandr";
// The numerals of the benchmark lengths.
import "./ladder-base.gandr";
// The negation composite and its transport `negVal`.
import "./negation-composite.gandr";

/// A hundred and one negations move `true` to `false`.
@[runs("+{.1 = *{}}")]
def negated100() -> Bool { negVal n100 }

/// A thousand and one negations move `true` to `false`.
@[runs("+{.1 = *{}}")]
def negated1000() -> Bool { negVal n1k }

/// A hundred thousand and one negations move `true` to `false`.
@[runs("+{.1 = *{}}")]
def negated100000() -> Bool { negVal n100k }
